post_install() {
    cat << EOF

==> wolf is installed. Check the build it names:

    wolf --version

    A release build prints the bare version and its pin —
    "wolf 0.2.6 (wolfgang, pin <sha>)". A "+dev" suffix means the
    binary was not built at its release tag (D57).

First program:

    printf 'fn main() {\n  print("hello, wolf")\n}\n' > hello.lu
    wolf run hello.lu

Native codegen (\`wolf build\` / \`wolf run\`) serves linux x86-64 today.
On linux aarch64 the native tier refuses BY NAME and the checked tier
still runs your program:

    wolf test hello.lu

Documentation:
--------------
    /usr/share/doc/wolf-lang/README.md
    https://github.com/wolffe-lang/wolf-lang/blob/v0.2.6/docs/platforms.md

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    cat << EOF

==> wolf has been upgraded. Confirm the build:

    wolf --version

EOF
}
